1. LICENSE RATE
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

W5D PHP CMS is licensed at 610.5 TND per hour of work.

Promotional offer valid before 2027 — strictly before 31 December 2026.
After that date, the standard rate applies.

The rate applies to:
  - Initial implementation and onboarding of a new deployment.
  - Custom templates, blocks, or modules built for a specific deployment.
  - Migrations, refactors, and feature additions requested by the licensee.
  - Integration work: payment gateways, SMS gateways, OAuth providers,
    external APIs.
  - Training, documentation, and support hours beyond the documented
    baseline.

A running total of hours × 610.5 TND must be visible on the owner
dashboard and in the license footer of every rendered page:

  "W5D Admin Dashboard licensed at 610.5 TND/hour of work.
   Promotional offer valid before 2027."

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
2. OPERATING DOCTRINE — 5% SAMPLING RULE
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The software enforces a 5% sampling rule on weekly reports:

  - Every week, 5% of submitted reports are randomly selected for
    re-review by the service leader or a delegate.
  - Selection is deterministic per (country_id, week_id) so the sample
    is reproducible.
  - Each sampled report is re-scored against the same rubric the
    manager used, and the result is recorded.
  - A sampled failure triggers the same rework path as a manager
    rejection.

The 5% rate is a fixed operating doctrine of this software. It is not
configurable from the owner dashboard, not editable in configuration
files, and not subject to per-country override. Any fork that changes
this rate must remove the W5D name and branding.

The 5% rate is published on the public status page (/status/) and on
each service page as part of the declared limits.

────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
3. HONESTY CONSTRAINT
────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

The figure "130,000 experts" is a DESIGN EQUATION:

  5 macro works × 26 services per macro work × 1,000 experts per
  service = 130,000.

It is NOT a claim that 130,000 experts are currently employed by W5D.
As of the date of this license:

  - The real footprint of W5D is 26 developers in Tunisia.
  - The number of certified W5D expert team members is 0.
  - "Live" in the status register does not mean "1,000 experts
    employed".

The software must not be deployed, marketed, or represented in a way
that contradicts this constraint. Every page that mentions the number
130,000 must link to the trust statement (/trust/statement/) and must
not promise a job. The linter enforces this constraint: any hard-coded
"130,000" or "2027" outside config/variables.php and
data/countries/tn.json fails the build.

